From f6763b1b412a9bc1449eedbb0dfcb1212ee64f28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Zack Garza" <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:53:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] refactor: one Lean provisioning script for the build
 and for an unpacked image

An image unpacked before the Lean repair cannot consume it without being
rebuilt, and a repair copied into a consumer would be a second implementation.
The Lean provisioning moves out of install-research-repositories.sh into
docker/provision-lean-packages.sh, which the build now calls, so an existing
image runs exactly what a rebuilt one runs.

The script walks a repository root, installs the toolchain each checkout pins
(a no-op where it is present), links the shared packages under
/opt/lake-packages into the packages directory each manifest resolves, keeps a
copy an image already carries when it is at the pinned revision -- an unpacked
Mathlib cache lives in one -- retrieves Mathlib's official cache only when the
image does not carry it, builds only the packages Mathlib imports, and stops
unless Mathlib.olean is present. No toolchain is added, no package is cloned
twice, and no checkout is edited.

Applied to the published unpacked image with the artifact bound in:

  docker/sage-image.py --rootfs ~/sage-image/rootfs run \
    --bind docker/provision-lean-packages.sh:/opt/provision-lean-packages.sh \
    --env ELAN_HOME=/opt/elan \
    -- /bin/bash /opt/provision-lean-packages.sh /repos

That run completed ("Build completed successfully (8709 jobs)"), and the
readback from the pinned project now prints
"Nat.add_comm : forall (n m : Nat), n + m = m + n".

It also reports a real collision it found rather than working around: the
checkouts share one packagesDir, and lean-cas-dsl pins lean_categories
eea5c7f3... while lean-cas-dsl-leaf-contracts pins 82d1370d..., so the shared
directory can only hold one of them. The script warns and leaves the copy in
place; it is not Mathlib's dependency and not the repair's to resolve.
